9. Since in this case certain facts are evident. This Court feels that it is a fit case for interference. The issues were framed properly, however, the same have not been appreciated with back grounds of the facts of this case. The facts which are evident from the record as well as discussion of the two sides are:--

(1) that as per clause 17 of the Nikahnama, jewelry was given to the petitioner as gift;

(2) that the petitioner was maltreated as a result of which she had to undergo for abortion;

(3) that from Poly Clinic Hospital, she never went back to the house of her in-laws;

(4) that the independent witness could not be dismantled even by the cross-examination established that it was more for the resistance by the respondent and his family that the reconciliation efforts could not succeed.
